cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite this repository and its fixed exposition version when using the article or experiments."
title: "What changes when the answer stays the same"
type: software
version: "submission-candidate-1"
authors:
  - family-names: "Soh"
    given-names: "Wei Meng"
    alias: "wms2537"
    affiliation: "Whyme Labs"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible exposition on Hadamard matrices, orthogonal changes of basis,
  and representation-dependent quantization error. The package contains an
  illustrated standalone article, an exact counterexample to universal
  improvement, paired synthetic experiments, a prespecified quantization
  group-size study, retained results, and independent verification code. It
  does not claim a solution of the Hadamard conjecture or a completed
  pretrained-model performance result.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Whyme-Labs/hadamard-exposition"
keywords:
  - "Hadamard matrix"
  - "Hadamard conjecture"
  - "orthogonal transformation"
  - "quantization"
  - "reproducible experiment"
  - "mathematical exposition"
